WEBVTT

00:06.006 --> 00:08.008
[opening theme music playing]

01:46.731 --> 01:49.025
[music fades]

01:49.109 --> 01:56.074
GYEONGSEONG CREATURE

01:59.244 --> 02:02.205
- [eerie music playing]
- [footsteps approaching]

02:28.606 --> 02:30.233
[sighs] What have you done?

02:31.734 --> 02:32.652
Mother.

02:34.445 --> 02:35.488
[moans]

02:36.489 --> 02:37.323
What have you done?

02:40.827 --> 02:41.953
Oh, Mother.

02:44.706 --> 02:46.624
[footsteps approaching]

02:48.418 --> 02:50.920
[breathing shakily]

02:52.797 --> 02:53.965
Master Jang.

03:05.727 --> 03:07.187
[Chae-ok] What happened to you?

03:08.104 --> 03:09.689
How badly are you hurt?

03:11.274 --> 03:12.442
Chae-ok, help me.

03:16.029 --> 03:18.531
[skin tearing]

03:29.292 --> 03:30.710
[Chae-ok gasping]

03:31.920 --> 03:33.963
[skin tearing continues]

03:40.345 --> 03:41.846
[gasping]

03:47.810 --> 03:48.853
Please, Master Jang.

03:53.650 --> 03:55.652
[gasping]

04:02.492 --> 04:04.244
[breathing heavily]

04:11.334 --> 04:13.336
[solemn music playing]

04:16.214 --> 04:17.465
[Tae-sang] Miss Yoon Chae-ok.

04:46.244 --> 04:47.620
Jang Tae-sang.

05:07.807 --> 05:11.144
GYEONGSEONG CREATURE
BETWEEN US AND THEM

05:11.227 --> 05:13.813
EPISODE 7
CHASE

05:13.896 --> 05:16.899
16 HOURS EARLIER

05:16.983 --> 05:19.777
All right, it's time.
Everyone, listen. We have ten minutes.

05:22.447 --> 05:24.949
[Tae-sang] When the truck pulls up,
we have ten minutes to escape.

05:25.033 --> 05:26.826
[unsettling music playing]

05:28.202 --> 05:30.621
Completely seal off the military ward
and block every entrance.

05:30.705 --> 05:31.706
[soldiers] Yes, sir!

05:39.297 --> 05:42.842
We all have to move quickly.
I don't want anyone to get left behind.

05:43.551 --> 05:46.012
What if we don't get everyone
into the truck on time?

05:46.763 --> 05:47.638
What happens then?

05:47.722 --> 05:51.392
The truck will still leave.
We have to save who we can. I'm sorry.

05:56.606 --> 05:58.691
All right. Are we all ready to do this?

06:17.585 --> 06:18.586
It's time.

06:20.088 --> 06:21.214
Let's get out of here.

06:28.471 --> 06:30.473
[liquid pouring]

06:31.224 --> 06:32.392
[chuckles]

06:34.977 --> 06:36.354
[slurping]

06:41.442 --> 06:42.985
[exhales]

06:43.486 --> 06:44.904
[Jung-won whispers] Careful.

06:55.748 --> 06:57.458
Let's have all the women go out first.

07:03.381 --> 07:04.590
[In-hyeok] Watch your step.

07:06.801 --> 07:07.927
Hold on tight.

07:09.387 --> 07:10.430
Be careful now.

07:12.640 --> 07:13.891
[Tae-sang] You can do this.

07:18.104 --> 07:19.188
[whimpers]

07:20.565 --> 07:21.649
[grunts]

07:30.992 --> 07:32.160
[Tae-sang] Easy now.

07:42.670 --> 07:45.381
They are wearing stolen uniforms
as a way to escape from here.

07:45.465 --> 07:47.800
Keep an eye out
for anyone that looks at all suspicious.

07:47.884 --> 07:50.011
- We need to find them.
- [soldiers] Yes, sir!

07:54.849 --> 07:56.017
[Haneda] What about this area?

07:57.477 --> 07:58.936
Has anyone searched this yet?

07:59.729 --> 08:03.024
Well, actually, three of our men
did enter a short while ago to look, sir.

08:06.402 --> 08:09.071
Then why are the lights
in the rooms turned off?

08:17.413 --> 08:18.873
[In-hyeok] You need to hurry up.

08:19.499 --> 08:20.750
If we delay any longer,

08:20.833 --> 08:23.628
we might not all get out of here,
so hurry. Just go.

08:24.462 --> 08:27.089
[Tae-sang] Go ahead, Myeong-ja. Careful.

08:27.673 --> 08:28.716
Hold on tight.

08:33.012 --> 08:34.013
[Tae-sang] Easy now.

08:37.266 --> 08:38.726
[grunts]

08:49.153 --> 08:51.280
What are you doing?
Why aren't you in line?

08:52.323 --> 08:53.449
Watching for soldiers.

08:53.533 --> 08:55.076
Didn't you hear
when I said women go first?

08:55.159 --> 08:56.994
I'm pretty sure
I made myself clear, didn't I?

08:58.371 --> 08:59.789
I said I'd do things my own way.

08:59.872 --> 09:02.208
Yes, you made yourself very clear,
but listen to me.

09:02.291 --> 09:04.001
I'll feel better
once you're in that truck.

09:04.085 --> 09:05.002
So go and get in line.

09:09.715 --> 09:11.133
Are you developing feelings for me?

09:19.100 --> 09:20.142
[scoffs]

09:21.561 --> 09:25.147
Um, why would you, uh, ask me
completely out of the blue like that?

09:26.232 --> 09:28.067
Needless to say, in a situation like this…

09:28.150 --> 09:32.530
If you're not developing feelings for me,
then forget any concerns that you have.

09:41.998 --> 09:43.499
- [gasps]
- [Jung-won] Careful.

09:44.125 --> 09:45.668
[whimpering]

09:45.751 --> 09:46.711
Careful now. Don't move.

09:47.587 --> 09:48.921
Shit!

09:49.005 --> 09:50.840
[gunshot]

09:52.258 --> 09:54.302
[unsettling music playing]

09:59.599 --> 10:02.518
You gotta go! Get out right now!
Get in your truck and get out of here!

10:02.602 --> 10:04.103
- Get out of here right now!
- Yes, sir!

10:12.486 --> 10:13.446
[body thuds]

10:21.829 --> 10:23.414
[Tae-sang] We have to go now. Hurry.

10:32.173 --> 10:33.090
Come on! Get out!

10:33.799 --> 10:36.719
- Let's go! Let's go! Let's move!
- [woman] Hurry! Hurry! Go, go, go!

10:36.802 --> 10:38.095
You're almost there.

10:41.599 --> 10:43.684
[Jung-won] I've got you.
There you go. Slowly.

10:54.403 --> 10:57.281
They're on the second floor!
Hurry up! Move! Let's go!

11:05.498 --> 11:07.875
[soldier] Move, move! Come on! Let's go!

11:18.094 --> 11:20.304
[whimpering]

11:23.349 --> 11:25.393
[sobs] What do we do now?

11:26.352 --> 11:27.937
It's my fault that they know we're here.

11:28.020 --> 11:29.522
[Chae-ok] It's not your fault.

11:29.605 --> 11:31.440
Don't blame yourself, okay?

11:32.441 --> 11:34.735
The Japanese soldiers
will come looking for us.

11:35.236 --> 11:36.487
They're gonna kill all of us.

11:36.570 --> 11:38.239
[Tae-sang] No one's going to die.

11:38.864 --> 11:40.449
Everybody's getting outta here.

11:40.533 --> 11:43.411
So how about you pull yourself together
for all our sakes?

11:44.787 --> 11:46.288
[crying]

11:52.294 --> 11:55.464
You should get to the truck.
I can hold them off on my own.

11:56.757 --> 11:58.467
Are you trying to act like
the lone big hero?

11:58.551 --> 12:00.636
I'm buying more time for us, so just go.

12:00.720 --> 12:04.098
No, I won't go. We'll hold them off first,
and then we'll escape together.

12:04.181 --> 12:06.976
[Tae-sang] Hey, aren't we
on the same side?

12:07.059 --> 12:09.228
Why do you always object
to everything that I tell you?

12:09.311 --> 12:12.148
We can be on the same side
and still disagree with each other.

12:13.149 --> 12:16.026
If I can't freely express
my difference in opinion with you,

12:16.527 --> 12:18.863
then I think the real problem here
is your ego.

12:19.655 --> 12:20.990
So just do as I say.

12:23.284 --> 12:24.410
[sighs]

12:32.042 --> 12:33.878
[unsettling music continues]

12:43.095 --> 12:44.138
Let me help with this.

12:46.182 --> 12:47.725
We should try and ration our bullets.

12:47.808 --> 12:50.019
If you can't make out a clear shot,
then don't shoot.

12:59.403 --> 13:01.405
[footsteps approaching]

13:04.742 --> 13:06.869
[tense music playing]

13:09.288 --> 13:11.540
[breathing heavily]

13:19.256 --> 13:21.217
No one is spared. Do you understand that?

13:21.300 --> 13:22.343
[all] Yes, sir!

13:22.426 --> 13:23.594
Soldiers, attack!

14:01.549 --> 14:04.885
Tell me. What exactly is happening
inside this hospital, Director?

14:06.095 --> 14:07.638
[breathes deeply]

14:07.721 --> 14:10.724
Are you quite certain you know nothing
about all the missing women lately?

14:11.308 --> 14:14.395
If you really want to know
what goes on inside of this hospital…

14:16.397 --> 14:19.108
you should first get permission
from the governor-general,

14:19.191 --> 14:20.401
as it is classified.

14:20.985 --> 14:24.947
Or you could return back home
and ask Lady Maeda yourself.

14:27.616 --> 14:28.993
What did you mean by that, huh?

14:30.703 --> 14:32.329
Well, what I meant by that was

14:32.413 --> 14:34.331
no outsiders are allowed to know anything

14:34.415 --> 14:36.709
that goes on inside
of Ongseong Hospital, Commissioner.

14:37.668 --> 14:38.502
And furthermore,

14:38.586 --> 14:40.921
not a single Josenjing man,
woman, or child

14:41.630 --> 14:44.633
gets to leave this hospital alive.
Discretion is a must.

14:44.717 --> 14:46.886
I'm not able to say
anything more than that.

14:47.386 --> 14:48.345
I hope you understand.

14:50.014 --> 14:51.599
And what if there is

14:51.682 --> 14:53.601
a Josenjing here
that I have been searching for?

14:57.813 --> 14:59.273
There can be no exceptions.

15:03.611 --> 15:04.945
[gunshots]

15:10.492 --> 15:12.244
Soldiers, cease your firing!

15:14.914 --> 15:16.707
[gunshots subside]

15:19.251 --> 15:20.085
Move in.

15:21.837 --> 15:23.839
[tense music continues]

15:35.267 --> 15:37.061
[gunshots]

15:40.105 --> 15:41.899
[angrily screams]

15:42.816 --> 15:44.568
They won't quit, those bastards.

15:49.114 --> 15:49.949
Are you injured?

15:50.032 --> 15:51.825
[breathing heavily]

15:53.327 --> 15:54.662
I just got grazed, is all.

15:55.329 --> 15:56.997
And what about you? Are you okay?

15:57.498 --> 15:58.958
I'm okay. I didn't get hit.

16:01.168 --> 16:02.378
And what about you over there?

16:03.420 --> 16:04.421
[rifle clatters]

16:04.505 --> 16:06.090
[gurgling]

16:08.550 --> 16:09.635
[clattering]

16:10.844 --> 16:11.762
[coughs]

16:12.346 --> 16:14.598
We need to get you out of here.
Try to get up.

16:15.391 --> 16:16.433
[Chae-ok grunts]

16:17.309 --> 16:18.936
- [Chae-ok breathing heavily]
- [gasps]

16:19.019 --> 16:21.605
Think about your mother.
I'm sure you miss her, right?

16:21.689 --> 16:23.774
If you wanna see her again,
let's get out of here.

16:23.857 --> 16:27.027
[Chae-ok sobs] Just stay with me.
Come on, get up. Please!

16:28.529 --> 16:30.531
[Chae-ok breathing heavily]

16:31.198 --> 16:33.075
[solemn music playing]

16:45.879 --> 16:47.715
It says Choi Yeong-gwan.

16:51.093 --> 16:51.969
[gasps]

16:53.846 --> 16:56.140
That's my… [gasps] …name.

16:57.641 --> 16:58.892
Please remember me.

17:01.520 --> 17:03.105
My address is

17:04.857 --> 17:06.984
9 Sangwangsimni-jung.

17:07.067 --> 17:08.527
[coughing]

17:18.370 --> 17:19.747
Please tell my mother…

17:22.708 --> 17:23.876
how much I…

17:26.628 --> 17:27.880
how much I miss her.

17:29.381 --> 17:31.133
[gasping]

17:32.134 --> 17:33.635
I said we'd escape together.

17:35.721 --> 17:37.306
Listen, I know you can do this.

17:37.890 --> 17:40.893
Your mother is waiting to see you again,
so let's get out of here, okay?

17:41.602 --> 17:43.937
Hey, just stay with me! Please!

17:44.021 --> 17:45.647
[Chae-ok crying] Please!

17:47.941 --> 17:49.943
[somber music playing]

17:57.951 --> 17:59.787
[breathes deeply]

18:06.168 --> 18:07.669
Chae-ok, don't blame yourself.

18:09.171 --> 18:10.547
They did this to him, not you.

18:11.799 --> 18:14.384
It's not fair what happened.
He didn't deserve this.

18:19.139 --> 18:20.849
Nobody deserves to die like this.

18:27.189 --> 18:30.692
Not those poor souls we lost earlier,
nor anyone imprisoned anywhere.

18:33.237 --> 18:34.863
My mother didn't deserve this.

18:35.572 --> 18:36.615
[sobs]

18:36.698 --> 18:38.158
I want to know why.

18:47.876 --> 18:50.420
[Tae-sang] We can't stay here.
We have to go.

18:51.130 --> 18:53.132
Even if we do get out of here alive…

18:56.677 --> 18:59.138
is there any hope out there for us at all?

18:59.638 --> 19:00.722
I can't say…

19:02.933 --> 19:04.852
but I won't give them the satisfaction

19:05.561 --> 19:07.020
of killing us.

19:07.104 --> 19:09.773
These guys aren't going to see
either of us die today.

19:13.360 --> 19:14.528
You see,

19:15.696 --> 19:18.198
I plan to survive their terror
as long as possible.

19:19.825 --> 19:20.826
I will live…

19:22.828 --> 19:26.748
just so I can continue to make their lives
hell for what they put us through.

19:28.208 --> 19:30.085
So I will just keep on surviving…

19:32.212 --> 19:33.922
so I can keep reminding them

19:35.382 --> 19:37.509
about everything those bastards did to us.

19:39.428 --> 19:40.512
I'm staying alive.

19:41.972 --> 19:44.183
I'm never giving up.
I'm fighting for all of us.

19:51.148 --> 19:52.524
[In-hyeok] Everyone made it down.

19:52.608 --> 19:54.484
You two better hurry over right now.

19:57.321 --> 20:00.240
It's time to go.
Just stick with me, all right?

20:13.295 --> 20:15.255
We need to force our way to gain entry.

20:15.797 --> 20:19.426
You will storm in there and exterminate
every person inside that room!

20:19.509 --> 20:21.136
- [all] Yes, sir!
- [man] Sergeant, wait.

20:31.813 --> 20:33.649
[Tae-sang] You go first. Be careful.

20:53.752 --> 20:55.087
See you soon, Master Jang.

21:15.065 --> 21:17.901
[tense music swells, subsides]

21:28.787 --> 21:30.122
[music fades]

21:30.205 --> 21:32.207
Master Jang, why don't you go down?

21:36.545 --> 21:37.462
Hey, what's wrong?

21:40.007 --> 21:43.343
Comrade Lee, one of us has to stay,
so I'll remain up here for now. You go.

21:45.804 --> 21:46.972
[Haneda] What's the meaning of this?

21:47.055 --> 21:49.433
Director Ichiro has sent orders
that the prisoners

21:49.516 --> 21:51.310
are all to be captured alive, Sergeant.

21:51.393 --> 21:52.894
Alive? What?

21:54.521 --> 21:56.440
But six of our own men
have already been killed!

21:56.523 --> 21:58.608
Well, I don't make the orders here now,
do I, Sergeant?

22:02.446 --> 22:04.281
We spare no one,
and that is a direct order!

22:04.364 --> 22:05.657
No, take them alive!

22:24.343 --> 22:25.260
[In-hyeok grunts]

22:43.487 --> 22:44.363
[sighs]

22:56.958 --> 23:00.921
What's going on? Where's Master Jang?
Why did he throw the rope down?

23:01.004 --> 23:02.672
Master Jang's not coming.

23:05.258 --> 23:07.010
[In-hyeok] Why does one of us
have to stay?

23:07.094 --> 23:09.638
In order for everyone on the truck
to leave this hospital safely,

23:09.721 --> 23:12.391
we need somebody here
to divert the Japanese soldiers away.

23:13.100 --> 23:14.059
What are you suggesting?

23:14.142 --> 23:16.853
Once you get down there,
don't wait for me. Just leave.

23:18.647 --> 23:20.982
I'll try to buy you
as much time as possible.

23:21.066 --> 23:23.068
Just get everyone out of here safely.

23:23.151 --> 23:25.153
[wistful music playing]

23:28.365 --> 23:30.784
No, we can't just leave
Master Jang behind.

23:30.867 --> 23:32.828
- This is what he wanted, okay?
- Get out of the way.

23:34.287 --> 23:36.081
[In-hyeok] Stop wasting time!
Get on the truck!

23:36.164 --> 23:37.207
I said get out of the way!

23:37.290 --> 23:38.959
[In-hyeok] You're gonna get
everyone killed!

23:40.043 --> 23:41.795
It will be your fault if we die.

23:55.225 --> 23:56.184
We have to go.

24:15.704 --> 24:16.830
[Mrs. Nawol] Mr. Gu.

24:18.707 --> 24:22.127
No matter what happens to you,
you need to leave on time,

24:23.670 --> 24:25.672
even if everyone isn't on the truck.

24:26.339 --> 24:28.925
That includes Master Jang.
Do you understand?

24:29.634 --> 24:32.971
Otherwise, this was for nothing.
Just get out of there.

24:34.806 --> 24:36.391
Where are you? I can't just…

24:39.144 --> 24:41.146
[sobbing]

24:41.229 --> 24:43.231
[engine starting]

24:46.651 --> 24:49.029
[crying]

24:58.205 --> 24:59.164
[sighs]

25:00.790 --> 25:02.792
[wistful music intensifies]

25:32.864 --> 25:33.865
[sighs]

25:37.369 --> 25:38.828
[music fades]

25:38.912 --> 25:40.413
I'll take full responsibility here.

25:40.497 --> 25:43.375
I'm the officer in charge,
so get in there and shoot them!

25:43.458 --> 25:44.960
Now you listen here, Sergeant!

25:45.961 --> 25:48.421
I can report everything
to Director Ichiro myself.

25:52.801 --> 25:55.512
Why are you standing there?
I said to attack!

25:55.595 --> 25:56.596
[soldiers] Yes, sir!

26:31.339 --> 26:32.424
[clicking]

26:32.507 --> 26:33.717
Shit.

26:40.599 --> 26:41.683
[grenade hissing]

26:45.854 --> 26:47.105
[gunshots continue]

26:52.235 --> 26:54.613
- [melancholy music playing]
- [gunshots continue]

26:58.908 --> 26:59.868
[rifles cock]

27:18.053 --> 27:20.055
[melancholy music continues]

28:09.771 --> 28:11.773
[melancholy music intensifies]

28:54.774 --> 28:56.067
[music fades]

29:03.742 --> 29:06.369
[Ishikawa] Once Akiko is rescued,
get rid of everyone else.

29:06.870 --> 29:08.079
[officer] Yes, sir.

29:15.336 --> 29:16.212
[car door closes]

29:16.296 --> 29:18.214
- Let's go.
- [officer] Yes, sir.

29:46.701 --> 29:47.869
[lamp squeaks]

29:52.332 --> 29:54.334
[unsettling music playing]

30:02.884 --> 30:04.928
Search every corner now!

30:05.011 --> 30:07.263
That means everyone! That's an order!

30:07.347 --> 30:10.141
- [tense music playing]
- [breathing heavily]

30:23.947 --> 30:25.281
[metallic clattering]

30:33.581 --> 30:36.167
- [music intensifies]
- [panting]

30:47.762 --> 30:49.264
[panting]

30:54.811 --> 30:55.854
[grunts]

30:56.563 --> 30:58.398
[soldier 1] There he is! That way!

31:00.483 --> 31:01.401
The intruder is heading

31:01.484 --> 31:03.862
towards the north side of the hospital
through the air shafts.

31:04.946 --> 31:07.490
- [tense music continues]
- [panting]

31:13.955 --> 31:15.290
[music intensifies]

31:18.751 --> 31:20.044
[grunts]

31:21.796 --> 31:23.548
- [loud clattering]
- [grunting]

31:32.432 --> 31:34.517
[music subsides]

31:54.120 --> 31:56.039
[man] I am certain of its authenticity.

31:56.122 --> 31:59.042
This piece was indeed crafted
in the late 18th century

31:59.125 --> 32:01.127
during the reign
of King Jeongjo the Great,

32:01.210 --> 32:03.046
the 22nd king of Joseon.

32:06.633 --> 32:09.135
[dialing]

32:12.096 --> 32:12.972
What's that?

32:14.891 --> 32:15.850
Ah.

32:16.601 --> 32:17.644
Are you sure?

32:20.688 --> 32:21.564
All right.

32:22.106 --> 32:23.441
Yes, I will do it, then.

32:28.279 --> 32:29.238
[sighs]

32:29.948 --> 32:31.699
They're taking quite a long time.

32:40.416 --> 32:42.043
Sir, look over there.

32:49.133 --> 32:50.510
[vehicle retreats]

32:55.515 --> 32:58.226
Young Master! Young Master!

32:58.309 --> 33:00.311
[Jun-taek whimpering]

33:01.187 --> 33:02.522
Please have mercy on me.

33:02.605 --> 33:04.399
- Don't kill me.
- Young Master, it's all right.

33:04.482 --> 33:07.360
Please have mercy on me.
I don't wanna die. I… I don't wanna--

33:07.443 --> 33:09.320
- [man] It's all right.
- Please don't kill me.

33:09.404 --> 33:10.738
[man] You're safe now, okay?

33:10.822 --> 33:12.824
[Jun-taek] Please! Please don't kill me.

33:13.449 --> 33:15.201
- Please have mercy on me.
- [breathing heavily]

33:15.284 --> 33:16.703
[Jun-taek] Please don't kill me.

33:16.786 --> 33:18.663
Please have mercy. I don't want…

33:18.746 --> 33:19.831
Please don't kill me!

33:19.914 --> 33:20.957
[breathing heavily]

33:23.084 --> 33:24.460
[intriguing music playing]

33:24.544 --> 33:25.503
Let's go.

33:57.827 --> 33:58.828
[car door closes]

34:03.041 --> 34:04.709
Ishikawa, is that you?

34:08.838 --> 34:10.131
Ishikawa!

34:10.214 --> 34:11.466
[Myeong-ja whimpers, pants]

34:36.741 --> 34:38.826
[Myeong-ja] I've missed you.
Thank you for saving me.

34:38.910 --> 34:41.120
I knew you would, Ishikawa. I did.

34:42.038 --> 34:43.164
Are you hurt anywhere?

34:46.793 --> 34:48.795
Our child is fine, Ishikawa.

34:49.378 --> 34:50.505
Wait, um,

34:51.380 --> 34:52.590
you should bathe first.

34:59.722 --> 35:00.640
[body thuds]

35:00.723 --> 35:02.809
[man] Please forgive me, Director Ichiro!

35:03.559 --> 35:07.814
When I… when I came to check on her,
the woman was already missing.

35:08.981 --> 35:11.234
If the woman was already missing,

35:11.317 --> 35:13.528
then how do you explain
getting locked inside her cell?

35:14.112 --> 35:15.530
Please forgive me! I'm deeply sorry!

35:17.240 --> 35:20.118
Director Ichiro,
Soma is the one who did this, sir.

35:20.701 --> 35:21.661
Soma?

35:28.167 --> 35:31.379
Yes, that's right!
I'm certain it was Sergeant Soma, sir.

35:32.839 --> 35:33.714
[man] Soma, help!

35:35.049 --> 35:35.967
Soma!

35:36.551 --> 35:38.052
Sir, please help me!

35:38.136 --> 35:39.178
Soma, please!

35:39.262 --> 35:41.597
- [man panting]
- [unsettling music playing]

35:46.853 --> 35:48.229
Soma, no!

35:49.272 --> 35:50.648
[body thuds]

35:50.731 --> 35:52.900
Soma, what a rat.

35:55.403 --> 35:56.404
Director Ichiro?

35:56.487 --> 35:57.780
Yes, what is it?

35:59.448 --> 36:01.367
[Kato] By any chance, did anyone here

36:02.827 --> 36:05.163
happen to drink what was in this glass?

36:05.246 --> 36:07.582
I didn't. I swear.
I was tied up the whole time.

36:07.665 --> 36:09.333
I didn't even know that glass was there.

36:09.417 --> 36:10.710
Then I wonder

36:11.752 --> 36:12.879
who it might've been.

36:12.962 --> 36:14.088
I don't know.

36:15.339 --> 36:16.841
I wasn't paying attention. I'm sorry.

36:17.842 --> 36:18.968
[Ichiro] Lt. Kato,

36:19.051 --> 36:22.013
I don't think you understand
how serious this situation is right now.

36:26.142 --> 36:27.894
I don't care who drank
from this cup of yours.

36:27.977 --> 36:29.604
That is not what is important, Lieutenant.

36:29.687 --> 36:32.356
All of the Joseon test subjects
we had imprisoned here are gone,

36:33.357 --> 36:35.526
including the woman
Lady Maeda entrusted us

36:35.610 --> 36:37.236
to keep safe within these walls.

36:37.737 --> 36:38.613
Do you understand?

36:45.620 --> 36:48.539
Go after that son of a bitch Soma,
right this instant!

36:49.582 --> 36:51.500
Return to the barracks
and stand by for orders.

36:51.584 --> 36:52.543
Yes, sir!

36:55.713 --> 36:57.423
- [Kato] Sergeant.
- Yes, sir.

36:57.506 --> 37:00.218
Who else did you say
entered this room again?

37:01.010 --> 37:02.136
Oh, it was, uh…

37:04.222 --> 37:05.473
Your clothes.

37:13.147 --> 37:13.981
[gasps]

37:14.065 --> 37:15.942
It was, uh, it was four people, sir.

37:19.195 --> 37:20.279
I see.

37:21.572 --> 37:22.657
That is all for now.

37:28.829 --> 37:29.872
[door closes]

37:34.877 --> 37:36.045
Who was it?

37:37.505 --> 37:39.507
Which unlucky person drank this?

37:41.926 --> 37:43.594
Who is infected?

37:43.678 --> 37:45.805
[mysterious music playing]

37:48.557 --> 37:50.184
[music fades]

38:10.830 --> 38:12.832
- [unsettling music playing]
- [groans]

38:16.002 --> 38:17.670
[groaning]

38:23.259 --> 38:24.218
[grunts]

38:24.760 --> 38:25.761
[gun clatters]

38:27.054 --> 38:28.848
[Haneda] I finally caught you.

38:30.433 --> 38:31.851
How about that?

38:38.858 --> 38:40.026
[gunshot]

38:40.776 --> 38:42.069
[gunshots]

38:43.779 --> 38:45.156
[gunshot echoing]

38:49.827 --> 38:51.829
[unsettling music playing]

39:17.688 --> 39:20.524
There's another truck
following close behind. What do we do?

39:32.536 --> 39:34.455
[unsettling music intensifies]

39:35.790 --> 39:37.124
[man] Watch out! Watch out!

39:42.546 --> 39:43.923
Get out of the way!

39:44.548 --> 39:46.258
- [man 2] Watch out!
- [woman screams]

40:02.441 --> 40:03.984
- Reverse the truck!
- Yes, sir!

40:14.954 --> 40:16.497
[tense music stops]

40:18.332 --> 40:20.835
- [crowd cheering]
- [festive music playing]

40:52.950 --> 40:55.077
- [loud explosion]
- [crowd cheering]

41:00.833 --> 41:03.961
Everyone, listen!
Everybody, enjoy yourselves.

41:04.044 --> 41:07.631
Everything is free tonight
because Master Jang is treating all of us.

41:07.715 --> 41:09.842
[cheering]

41:09.925 --> 41:11.510
[Yeong-chun] Come over this way, please.

41:12.011 --> 41:13.762
- [man] Is it free?
- Everything's free tonight.

41:13.846 --> 41:15.556
Enjoy it, good sir. Here, take this.

41:15.639 --> 41:17.725
- Over here! Here you go!
- [man 2] Come over this way!

41:17.808 --> 41:20.519
Yes, absolutely! Have a free beer!
Have as much as you want!

41:20.603 --> 41:23.481
- [man 2] Drink up!
- [man 1] Yes, over here! Come this way!

41:28.777 --> 41:30.446
[unsettling music playing]

41:37.119 --> 41:38.204
We're losing him.

41:40.748 --> 41:41.957
Hey, reverse the truck.

41:42.041 --> 41:44.502
We can catch him on the side road
if we hurry. Let's go now!

41:55.387 --> 41:57.556
All of you! Get out of the way now!

41:57.640 --> 41:59.934
Oh, sorry, Officer. I'm sorry about that.

42:02.478 --> 42:04.230
Come on, let's go! They're leaving!

42:04.855 --> 42:07.024
[crowd cheering]

42:07.107 --> 42:09.485
We better hurry,
or they'll disappear from our sight!

42:09.568 --> 42:10.736
- Let's go!
- Yes, sir.

42:10.819 --> 42:12.821
[unsettling music intensifies]

42:35.052 --> 42:37.304
[unsettling music intensifies]

42:52.069 --> 42:53.612
- Get out.
- Huh?

42:53.696 --> 42:56.740
I, um… But I'm supposed
to deliver this truck.

42:56.824 --> 42:57.950
I said get out!

42:58.033 --> 42:58.909
Okay, I will,

42:59.577 --> 43:02.538
but I'm just following
what Commissioner Ishikawa said, huh?

43:05.457 --> 43:06.292
[grunts]

43:12.047 --> 43:13.215
Who are you hiding back there?

43:13.299 --> 43:15.593
I don't know what you mean.
The back of where, huh?

43:16.552 --> 43:17.720
The back of this truck, or…

43:18.554 --> 43:21.515
I dropped off Myeong-ja as instructed,
and nobody else climbed in.

43:21.599 --> 43:22.600
I promise you, Officer.

43:22.683 --> 43:24.268
Are you sure?

43:28.397 --> 43:29.982
[people screaming]

43:30.065 --> 43:31.859
[man] What was that? What's going on?

43:32.526 --> 43:35.404
Officer, don't! What are you doing?
Civilians are watching.

43:42.369 --> 43:43.704
Where are they, huh?

43:44.455 --> 43:46.081
Where did the prisoners go, huh?

43:47.416 --> 43:50.669
You were smuggling prisoners in there,
so tell us what you did with them now!

43:56.634 --> 43:58.260
Officer, I told you already.

43:59.762 --> 44:02.431
Myeong-ja was the only individual
from the hospital we took.

44:03.557 --> 44:05.976
Commissioner Ishikawa
requested her and nobody else.

44:06.977 --> 44:09.396
So we have fulfilled our promise
to the commissioner.

44:09.980 --> 44:11.649
What is the problem, Officer?

44:12.816 --> 44:14.193
[crowd cheering]

44:21.033 --> 44:22.034
[gasps]

44:27.956 --> 44:29.583
Hurry and change your clothes.

44:29.667 --> 44:32.002
- [dramatic music playing]
- [woman] We're gonna get out of here.

44:32.086 --> 44:33.712
[waiter] Drink up! Have fun!

44:37.549 --> 44:39.677
Oh, sorry, Officer! I'm sorry about that.

44:45.766 --> 44:47.685
[jazz music playing]

44:53.774 --> 44:55.275
[dramatic music soars]

45:05.369 --> 45:07.830
[man 1] Careful. Careful now.

45:20.175 --> 45:22.511
We better hurry,
or they'll disappear from our sight!

45:22.594 --> 45:23.637
- Let's go!
- Yes, sir!

45:39.278 --> 45:40.988
[music subsides]

45:44.241 --> 45:47.077
We are relieved
that you made it out safely in one piece.

45:47.745 --> 45:49.955
With that said,
I'm afraid time is really not on our side.

45:50.038 --> 45:51.665
You must hurry out of town this instant.

45:52.374 --> 45:54.126
- [Jung-won] Quickly now.
- [woman] Let's go.

45:57.504 --> 45:59.006
[woman] Thank you so much.

45:59.089 --> 46:00.591
[In-hyeok] You have to go. Be safe.

46:00.674 --> 46:02.342
[woman] Hurry. Let's go.
I'll see you there.

46:03.427 --> 46:04.428
[In-hyeok] Excuse me, but…

46:05.929 --> 46:07.723
are you with the House of Golden Treasure?

46:10.768 --> 46:12.019
I'm sorry to report this.

46:13.312 --> 46:15.230
Master Jang did not make it out
of the hospital.

46:17.733 --> 46:20.360
You get home safely now and be careful.

46:20.444 --> 46:22.321
I wanted to ask you something
if that's okay.

46:24.198 --> 46:26.200
Was this Master Jang's plan from…

46:27.826 --> 46:29.953
from the beginning,
or was this all of your own doing?

46:31.538 --> 46:33.457
You must not know this yet,

46:33.540 --> 46:37.169
but anyone who needs anything
in Gyeongseong seeks out Master Jang,

46:37.252 --> 46:40.130
whether it's money,
a favor, or a missing person.

46:40.881 --> 46:43.175
Master Jang has a big hand in everything.

46:44.051 --> 46:45.928
He helps his people more than anyone.

46:46.428 --> 46:47.805
That is the man he is.

46:49.807 --> 46:50.766
[sighs]

46:57.523 --> 46:59.191
Sir, you're under arrest!

47:02.653 --> 47:03.904
[unsettling music playing]

47:04.613 --> 47:07.115
I want everyone to spread out
and find those prisoners!

47:07.616 --> 47:09.910
Arrest anyone that looks suspicious.
That's a direct order!

47:09.993 --> 47:11.328
Now hurry up and move!

47:11.411 --> 47:12.412
[officers] Yes, sir!

47:13.413 --> 47:14.456
[people scream]

47:14.540 --> 47:16.291
[cheering]

47:18.043 --> 47:20.045
- [gunshots]
- [people screaming]

47:29.429 --> 47:30.681
Put everything away!

47:31.431 --> 47:33.433
[people screaming, clamoring]

47:44.111 --> 47:45.863
[girl crying]

47:47.865 --> 47:48.991
[screaming]

47:55.247 --> 47:56.874
[grunts, screams]

48:20.606 --> 48:22.316
[music subsides]

48:27.154 --> 48:29.156
[solemn music playing]

48:51.178 --> 48:52.346
[bell jingles]

49:12.574 --> 49:14.618
[music soars]

49:23.543 --> 49:26.755
[Tae-sang] Till the cherry blossoms
lose their flowers.

49:37.474 --> 49:39.017
Do you think he's still alive?

49:40.894 --> 49:42.896
[wistful music playing]

50:06.253 --> 50:07.879
[pensive music playing]

50:11.174 --> 50:12.426
[wind chime rattles]

50:24.771 --> 50:27.733
Your husband just sent word
he is working late again.

50:27.816 --> 50:31.695
So he won't be returning home
until very late tonight, it seems.

50:46.126 --> 50:48.128
[intriguing music playing]

51:02.476 --> 51:03.560
[chuckles]

51:30.420 --> 51:32.130
[Ichiro] My apologies, Lady Maeda.

51:32.798 --> 51:34.841
I am deeply ashamed.

51:35.675 --> 51:39.513
[Maeda] I have already given you
several chances, Director Ichiro.

51:39.596 --> 51:40.430
Have I not?

51:41.890 --> 51:44.726
You asked for a hospital,
so I built one for you.

51:44.810 --> 51:49.231
You needed funding for your experiments,
so I spared no expense in my support.

51:49.898 --> 51:52.400
I… I will rectify this situation,
no matter what it takes.

51:52.484 --> 51:53.652
You have my word, I promise.

51:53.735 --> 51:54.986
And how will you do that?

51:55.070 --> 51:56.696
All of your test subjects escaped,

51:56.780 --> 51:59.449
so just how are you planning
on recapturing them?

52:00.659 --> 52:02.869
And Akiko has completely disappeared.

52:04.621 --> 52:06.832
How will you find her, Director?

52:06.915 --> 52:08.542
Uh, I, uh…

52:08.625 --> 52:10.794
Very soon I will draw up a plan, um…

52:10.877 --> 52:13.797
I just… If I could have some time,
I'll take responsibility and--

52:13.880 --> 52:15.006
You will resign.

52:18.635 --> 52:22.222
You will step down from your position,
Director Ichiro,

52:23.056 --> 52:25.058
and then you will return to Tokyo at once.

52:32.691 --> 52:36.236
Before you go, we had success
in a significant experiment.

52:44.536 --> 52:46.580
We've created a valuable organism

52:47.205 --> 52:49.082
that will shake up the medical world.

52:49.166 --> 52:50.500
I also think it could, uh,

52:51.168 --> 52:54.045
possibly change the course
of human history as we know it.

52:54.129 --> 52:57.591
I assure you that you will not be
disappointed with me this time.

52:58.341 --> 53:00.594
May I be given another chance, please?

53:01.428 --> 53:02.470
Please, Lady Maeda.

53:02.554 --> 53:04.556
[unsettling music playing]

53:50.227 --> 53:51.811
[Ichiro] Yes, that's her.

53:52.395 --> 53:55.065
She is the Josenjing woman
you asked me to take special care of

53:55.148 --> 53:56.149
all those years ago.

53:56.900 --> 53:58.443
She is the experiment.

54:05.283 --> 54:07.285
[brooding music playing]

54:22.676 --> 54:24.678
[music subsides]

54:27.722 --> 54:29.724
[officer] The specimen
has been successfully sedated

54:29.808 --> 54:31.309
and securely locked in a cage for now.

54:31.393 --> 54:33.478
How much more nitrogen
do you think is needed, sir?

54:36.606 --> 54:37.440
Lt. Kato.

54:39.192 --> 54:40.318
I wonder,

54:41.278 --> 54:43.363
who was the one who drank this?

54:53.707 --> 54:55.709
[tense music playing]

54:57.794 --> 54:59.796
[bell ringing]

55:04.342 --> 55:06.511
- [Soma] Hurry, get in! Get in!
- [woman] Okay. Okay.

55:10.473 --> 55:12.475
[tense music continues]

55:27.073 --> 55:28.199
[grunts]

55:31.077 --> 55:32.579
[breathing heavily]

55:35.415 --> 55:36.958
[grunts]

55:39.502 --> 55:40.879
[groans]

55:53.058 --> 55:55.435
[labored breathing]

55:58.938 --> 56:00.190
[groans]

56:03.443 --> 56:04.736
[Kato] I wonder who

56:05.528 --> 56:06.780
drank from the glass.

56:07.739 --> 56:09.407
Who swallowed the Najin?

56:16.831 --> 56:19.793
[tense music swells, fades]

56:25.590 --> 56:27.842
[soothing music playing]

57:05.630 --> 57:07.048
[sobs]

57:18.977 --> 57:21.312
- [wistful music playing]
- [crying]

57:26.317 --> 57:28.153
[crying, sniffles]

57:38.872 --> 57:41.624
[crying]

57:56.764 --> 57:58.766
[crying continues]

58:01.311 --> 58:03.146
[music fades]

58:17.911 --> 58:19.913
[eerie music playing]

58:21.915 --> 58:23.082
[skin squelching]

58:30.465 --> 58:32.467
[ominous music playing]

58:36.346 --> 58:38.348
[music swells]

58:38.431 --> 58:39.849
[fades]

58:41.226 --> 58:43.228
["Forever" by SUHO playing]

58:47.023 --> 58:48.191
♪ Stuck in my head ♪

58:48.274 --> 58:50.276
♪ I've been searchin' for the reason ♪

58:52.987 --> 58:54.989
♪ Nameless longing ♪

58:55.073 --> 58:57.534
♪ I've been waitin' for you for so long ♪

58:57.617 --> 58:58.868
♪ For so long ♪

58:58.952 --> 59:00.495
♪ But got no direction ♪

59:00.578 --> 59:02.872
♪ No matter, I wanna reach you ♪

59:03.873 --> 59:06.751
♪ Another way you runnin'
Goin' on and on ♪

59:06.834 --> 59:08.670
♪ But need a way to get to you ♪

59:11.130 --> 59:12.966
♪ You ♪

59:13.591 --> 59:16.219
♪ You know I'm so stuck with you ♪

59:16.302 --> 59:17.220
♪ No, oh, oh ♪

59:17.303 --> 59:18.972
♪ You ♪

59:19.597 --> 59:22.267
♪ Baby, I don't care at all ♪

59:22.350 --> 59:25.270
♪ You'll never know what I could do ♪

59:25.353 --> 59:27.981
♪ You'll never know
What we could have been ♪

59:28.064 --> 59:29.983
♪ For you, no, oh, oh, oh ♪

59:30.066 --> 59:31.067
♪ Oh, oh ♪

59:31.150 --> 59:33.027
♪ Do you know? ♪

59:33.111 --> 59:34.112
♪ Oh, no ♪

59:34.195 --> 59:35.989
♪ All the way I found you here ♪

59:36.072 --> 59:37.031
♪ Oh, oh ♪

59:37.115 --> 59:39.033
♪ Oh, I'll be right back for you ♪

59:39.117 --> 59:40.076
♪ Oh, no ♪

59:40.159 --> 59:41.953
♪ All the way I found you here ♪

59:42.036 --> 59:42.996
♪ Oh, oh ♪

59:43.079 --> 59:44.998
♪ Oh, I'll be right back for you ♪

59:45.081 --> 59:46.249
♪ Oh, no ♪

59:50.044 --> 59:51.254
♪ Chasing the lights ♪

59:51.337 --> 59:53.423
♪ Even don't know where I'm goin' ♪

59:55.925 --> 59:57.885
♪ Losing my sight ♪

59:57.969 --> 01:00:00.555
♪ Hope you know
That what I'm looking for ♪

01:00:01.973 --> 01:00:03.433
♪ But got no direction ♪

01:00:03.516 --> 01:00:05.977
♪ No matter, I wanna reach you ♪

01:00:06.894 --> 01:00:09.814
♪ Another way you runnin'
Goin' on and on ♪

01:00:09.897 --> 01:00:11.733
♪ But need a way to get to you ♪

01:00:14.068 --> 01:00:17.322
♪ Ride on a paper plane ♪

01:00:19.949 --> 01:00:23.536
♪ Sandcastles on a seaside ♪

01:00:24.454 --> 01:00:26.080
♪ Don't scare me at all ♪

01:00:26.164 --> 01:00:28.958
♪ If I can get on with you forever ♪

01:00:29.042 --> 01:00:31.836
♪ Just wanna be there with you forever ♪

01:00:33.504 --> 01:00:36.007
♪ How beauty miserable us ♪

01:00:36.591 --> 01:00:38.092
♪ Let me keep on ♪

01:00:38.176 --> 01:00:40.303
♪ Know what I could do ♪

01:00:40.386 --> 01:00:42.972
♪ You'll never know
What we could have been ♪

01:00:43.056 --> 01:00:44.974
♪ For you, no, oh, oh, oh, oh ♪

01:00:45.058 --> 01:00:45.933
♪ Oh, oh ♪

01:00:46.017 --> 01:00:48.019
♪ Do you know? ♪

01:00:48.102 --> 01:00:49.145
♪ Oh, no ♪

01:00:49.228 --> 01:00:51.064
♪ All the way I found you here ♪

01:00:51.147 --> 01:00:52.023
♪ Oh, oh ♪

01:00:52.106 --> 01:00:54.025
♪ Oh, I'll be right back for you ♪

01:00:54.108 --> 01:00:55.109
♪ Oh, no ♪

01:00:55.193 --> 01:00:57.028
♪ All the way I found you here ♪

01:00:57.111 --> 01:00:58.071
♪ Oh, oh ♪

01:00:58.154 --> 01:00:59.989
♪ Oh, I'll be right back for you ♪

01:01:00.073 --> 01:01:01.324
♪ Oh, no ♪

01:01:02.158 --> 01:01:05.870
♪ Lead me to the way towards you ♪

01:01:07.705 --> 01:01:10.249
♪ I've been waitin' for so long ♪

01:01:10.333 --> 01:01:13.252
♪ I'm ready to run to you ♪

01:01:14.087 --> 01:01:17.048
♪ Reason for another reason ♪

01:01:17.131 --> 01:01:20.259
♪ Now I'm so sick of waitin' ♪

01:01:20.760 --> 01:01:22.428
♪ Voice in my head ♪

01:01:23.054 --> 01:01:26.140
♪ Mess around in my mind ♪

01:01:26.224 --> 01:01:28.393
♪ Know what I could do ♪

01:01:28.476 --> 01:01:30.978
♪ You'll never know
What we could have been ♪

01:01:31.062 --> 01:01:33.064
♪ For you, no, oh, oh, oh, oh ♪

01:01:33.147 --> 01:01:34.023
♪ Oh, oh ♪

01:01:34.107 --> 01:01:36.025
♪ Do you know? ♪

01:01:36.109 --> 01:01:37.318
♪ Oh, no ♪

